            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0398" n="390" sameAs="frus:frus1941v04/pg390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/2186: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-08-22T14:00:00+09:00">August 22, 1941—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 22—4:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1286. For the Secretary and the Under Secretary only. Embassy’s 1267, August 18,
                    9 p.m. The Minister for Foreign Affairs sent me word this morning through the
                    Director of the American Bureau that the German Ambassador had yesterday called
                    on Admiral Toyoda and had asked what was the subject of the conversation which I
                    had with Admiral Toyoda on August 18, and that Admiral Toyoda had informed the
                    German Ambassador that I had called to make representations with regard to a
                    number of specific cases of difficulties experienced by Americans in Japan and
                    China.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
